diff --git a/packages/apps/README.md b/packages/apps/README.md
index b398f7f..49f1efc 100644
--- a/packages/apps/README.md
+++ b/packages/apps/README.md
@@ -98,6 +98,30 @@ handler that declares its context without a type gets the caller's, with
 schedules (`userCron`, `userInterval`) run once for each member who enables them,
 as them. `{ accounts }` requirements and `ctx.accounts` are removed.
 
+An app can accept accounts from its users with an explicit app requirement:
+
+```ts
+{ app: { accounts: { subscriptions: provider.many().contributed() } } }
+```
+
+Only app requirements can be contributed. The deployment records `contributed`
+beside `cardinality`, defaulting to `false` for existing requirements. Members
+who can use the app may connect or link an account they can use. Contributors
+may remove their own links; app editors may remove any link. Normal app
+requirements stay manager-only. A member's personal contributions are queued
+for cleanup when they leave or are removed from the organization. Cleanup runs
+after membership removal commits and retries independently. An app-acquired
+account's `remove` handler runs before its reference is deleted. Make `remove`
+idempotent, because a process can stop after the external removal but before
+the host records its result.
+
+App link views include `linkedBy: { id, name }` and `canRemove`; requirement views
+include `canContribute`. Other app users see availability, health and usage,
+without upstream identity or plan badges. Status badges and stats are private by default.
+Set `identity: false` only on a badge or stat safe for other app users, such as
+`{ label: "Available", tone: "good", identity: false }`. The account's holder and
+app editors see all badges, stats and upstream identity. Usage meters remain shared.
+
 Authenticated templates use a `provider.many()` user requirement and
 `accountRouter` from `apps`. A factory also runs without a caller for app-scope
 work, so `ctx.user` may be undefined there:
